# ACIT Gateway

Deterministic, test-mode bridge for agentic commerce. An Agent presents a
Protocol envelope (AP2/TAP/P3P/UAP); the Gateway verifies the Mandate,
sanitizes IDPI via the Firewall, enforces Guardrails, then runs a Razorpay
test-mode Money action or a Refusal, and writes a SHA-256 hash-chained
Audit event.

## Pointers (read when the branch fires)

- Terminology — `docs/CONTEXT.md` (Mandate, Agent, Firewall, Guardrail,
  Refusal, Money action; `InternalMandate` aliases `Mandate`)
- Agent instructions + build phases — `docs/AGENTS.md`
- Coding/testing/security/git — `docs/RULES.md`
- Spec — `docs/SPEC.md`; scope — `docs/PRD.md`
- Architecture — `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`; phases — `docs/PHASES.md`
- Progress — `docs/MEMORY.md`; decisions — `docs/adr/`

## Hard constraints

- Python 3.11+, FastAPI, Pydantic v2, SQLModel, PyJWT, SQLite, Docker.
- Razorpay test-mode keys only. ₹0 budget.
- No LLM on the runtime path (ADR-0002). Agents are clients.
- All external input untrusted until Firewall passes.
- Conventional commits. Do not push unless asked.
